{
 "contract": "relata.problem-details-fixtures/v1",
 "about": "Wire-exact RFC 9457 responses captured from a live relata serve (non-synthetic cases carry a `live` request that the Rust test http_e2e::contract_matrix::problem_fixtures_match_live_server replays against the real binary), plus a few synthetic shapes. Every SDK (python, typescript, go) must map each case to the same error kind, status, code, type, retryable flag, request id and retry delay. kinds: purpose|auth|forbidden|not_found|conflict|precondition_failed|validation|rate_limited|server|bad_request|other. Go has no sentinel for purpose/bad_request/other. Env groups: default={}, queue_full={RELATA_OTLP_ENABLED=true,RELATA_INGEST_QUEUE_MAX_BYTES=1}, disk_pressure={RELATA_OTLP_ENABLED=true,RELATA_MIN_FREE_DISK_MB=1073741824}, acl_denied={RELATA_ACL_GRANT_HTTP=PermittedDoc:read,AclFixtureDoc:write} (the caller may write but not read AclFixtureDoc, #5696). The 410 case is the tombstone of a removed surface: an old client keeps the server's remediation text (the replacement route), tested in all three SDKs and replayed live.",
 "cases": [
  {
   "name": "unauthorized_401",
   "live": {
    "method": "GET",
    "path": "/v1/audit/count",
    "authed": false,
    "group": "default"
   },
   "wire": {
    "status": 401,
    "headers": {
     "content-type": "application/problem+json",
     "www-authenticate": "Bearer realm=\"relata\"",
     "x-request-id": "req-unauthorized_401"
    },
    "body": {
     "type": "about:blank",
     "title": "Unauthorized",
     "status": 401,
     "detail": "Unauthorized",
     "code": "about:blank",
     "request_id": "req-unauthorized_401"
    }
   },
   "expect": {
    "kind": "auth",
    "status": 401,
    "code": "about:blank",
    "type": "about:blank",
    "retryable": false,
    "request_id": "req-unauthorized_401",
    "retry_after_seconds": null
   }
  },
